// Le03 1.21a practice port.
// Native-menu interaction derived from Priw8 prac.cea v0.2.
// Stage/pattern research: leprac, Oscar; phase skips: RosePenguin100.
// Target SHA-256: 955cd8fe51cd95813decf1d429578b9844a63ef9a5b8ebf048be5c2322ca1426
//   (original Japanese v1.21a -- window title ends in ".ver 1.21a")
// The Chinese-translated v1.20a (87563980...40c44a) also works: the two builds
// differ only by a 16-byte relocation inside .rdata, so every site below lands
// on the same bytes.  With a 1.20a base exactly one assert mismatches --
// game+827B2, the string pointer 68 f0 77 86 00 vs 68 e0 77 86 00 -- which
// build.py downgrades to a warning via --lenient.  Verified 2026-10-16: the
// cave produced from either base is byte-identical.
// CE: attach to the prepared Le03prac.exe; enable before entering practice.
// All numeric literals are hexadecimal. Do not apply to another version.
//
// v0.5.19 -- the overlay now leaves the game completely alone while a replay
//            or an attract demo is playing back: no back-buffer writes (the
//            markers) and no hint-file I/O (the self-heal in ovl_mirror).
//            A replay is FRAME-INDEXED -- each 0x44-byte record carries the
//            game frame number it belongs to and the game looks records up by
//            that number -- so extra work on that path can shift the frame
//            sequence and desync it.  See `desync分析.md`; the gate is the one
//            the v0.5.9d diagnostic build proved out.
//            Also FIX: OVL_SWATCH had six entries but the main table has had
//            seven rows since v0.5.18, so the Hit row read one dword past the
//            array (it happened to hit OVL_SWATCH2[0] == 0).
//
// v0.5.18 -- Lock Power splits into Lock P1 / Lock P2.  Le03 is the only one
//            of the three games with two characters, and the player object
//            carries a power value for each: +0x7C (main) and +0x80 (partner).
//            The vanilla code clamps the pair in the same function -- +0x7C at
//            game+E076B (our hook) and +0x80 at game+E078C -- so the single
//            hook drives both, each with its own latch and target.  Main menu
//            6 -> 7 rows; Le01/Le02 keep one Lock Power row because they have
//            one power value.
//
// v0.5.17 -- the hint settings panel title is now "F12 - HINT (ESC: back)",
//            the same string Le01/Le02 use.  v0.5.15 had invented
//            "HINT SETTINGS", which made the three panels the one place they
//            still differed -- and it dropped the only on-screen hint that ESC
//            leaves the panel.
//
// v0.5.16 -- FIX: the hint markers (and the Player+ cross) were drawn ~162 px
//            too far LEFT and ~28 px too far UP.  v0.5.15 moved the Fix X/Y
//            rows from quarter to eighth logical units, which means doubling
//            the shift, the Fix bias AND the divisor -- but HINT_OXQ /
//            HINT_OYQ (the playfield origin) were left at their quarter-unit
//            values, so the origin term alone came out halved.  Both are now
//            780 / 136.  At neutral Fix the mapping is once again IDENTICAL
//            to v0.5.14's, which is the acceptance test.
//
// v0.5.15 -- the hint/menu port (Le01 v0.1.9/v0.1.10 parity).  The F12 menu
//            splits into a 6-row main table and a 10-row HINT SETTINGS panel
//            (Z on the Hint row opens it, ESC backs out); Hint col / P+ size /
//            P+ col are new; colour rows walk 12 presets with left/right and
//            type a 6-digit hex value with Z; the panel shows a colour swatch
//            and prints colour rows as RRGGBB.  hint files gain an OPTIONAL
//            seventh-to-ninth column (R G B, same line) and Fix X/Y move from
//            quarter to EIGHTH logical units (neutral 128, range 0..256), so
//            one count is ~0.4 px.  prac.cfg becomes table-driven with seven
//            keys.  cave grows 0x8000 -> 0x10000 for the extra code.
//
// v0.5.11 -- FIX: Alpha (stage 8) showed Pattern = -1 for the whole stage.
//            ovl_mirror's stage-number liveness test was written as 1..7, but
//            Le03 has eight stage entries -- stage 7 is Extra and stage 8 is
//            Alpha.  The bound is now 1..8.  Details at the test itself.
//
// v0.5.10 -- FIX: seed_hook read the wrong stack slot.  The game's seed is
//            pushed just before the call, so after pushfd + 5 pushes it sits
//            at [esp+1C] (28 decimal) -- but the hook said [esp+28], i.e. hex
//            0x28 = 40, which is 12 bytes too far.  With Lock Seed OFF (the
//            default) the RNG was therefore seeded from a stale stack dword
//            instead of the game's own seed, which desynchronises replay
//            playback and makes boss patterns differ from the recording.
//            Locking the seed masked the bug because that path overwrites
//            the value anyway.
//
// v0.5.8  -- hint cross now shares the player cross's transform (Fix X/Y was
//            applied TWICE to the player cross and never to the hints, so the
//            two disagreed by 5*(Fix-64) quarter units); hint_load moved from
//            beginPracticeStage to initFrameTimer, where Le02 has it, so it
//            always sees the live stage object; ovl_mirror self-heals
//            HINT_WANT if it ever stops matching the stage being played.
define(game,"Le03prac.exe")
define(cave,game+BE8000)
define(DIFF,game+B0A53C)
define(CHAR_IDX,game+B0A540)
define(getInput,game+82BC0)
define(getTextTexture,game+117DD0)
define(drawTextTexture,game+11EAA0)
define(KEY_DOWN,KEYS+0)
define(KEY_LEFT,KEYS+4)
define(KEY_RIGHT,KEYS+8)
define(KEY_UP,KEYS+C)
define(KEY_Z,KEYS+10)
define(KEY_X,KEYS+14)
define(KEY_SHIFT,KEYS+18)
define(HINT_NUMX,14D)
define(HINT_NUMY,190)
define(HINT_DEN,190)
define(HINT_SCALE,9C40)
define(HINT_QSCALE,4E200)
// "a replay is playing": replay object 0xF04578, byte +5.
define(REPLAY_FLAG,F0457D)

[ENABLE]
assert(game+827B2,68 e0 77 86 00)
assert(game+10B52F,e8 9c d8 06 00)
assert(game+1F3EBC,e8 0f 6e fc ff)
assert(game+16DEB8,68 00 01 00 00)
assert(game+E0291,83 78 48 00 7f 37)
assert(game+E076B,8b 07 83 78 7c 00 7d 07 c7 40 7c 00 00 00 00 8b 07 81 78 7c f4 01 00 00 7c 07 c7 40 7c f4 01 00 00)
assert(game+D8D9B,e8 20 32 02 00)
assert(game+D883E,8b f9 0f 57 c0)
assert(game+D949F,c7 47 4c 00 00 00 00)
assert(game+29F20,89 06 e8 a8 11 2c 00)
assert(game+2BC8B,8b 8f d4 00 00 00)
assert(game+DCBA6,e8 75 14 03 00)
assert(game+D9A8C,c7 87 34 28 00 00 00 00 00 00)
assert(game+DF6AE,c7 40 58 00 00 00 00)
assert(game+EC1E0,8b 46 4c 3b 46 6c)
assert(game+EC219,6a 00 ff 76 30)
assert(game+EC1EC,83 7e 30 08 0f 84 92 00 00 00)
assert(game+EC223,e8 c8 4f f2 ff)
assert(game+EEB44,80 bb a5 00 00 00 01)
assert(game+EEDB9,80 bb a5 00 00 00 01)
assert(game+EEEE4,80 bb a5 00 00 00 01)
assert(game+EF067,80 bb a5 00 00 00 01)
assert(game+EF221,80 bb a5 00 00 00 00)
assert(game+28F22,c7 83 e0 09 00 00 70 17 00 00)
assert(game+2B1AD,c7 40 6c 00 00 00 00)
assert(game+71892,81 ff b0 04 00 00 74 18)
assert(game+FE5B,c7 46 08 00 00 00 00)
assert(game+FF18,e8 ff a7 2d 00)
assert(game+FE08,e8 d2 b5 2d 00)
assert(game+1924,e8 b7 94 0f 00)
assert(game+214CE3,b8 df b0 08 99)
assert(game+DF672,c7 40 48 03 00 00 00)
assert(game+DF681,8b 84 87 c0 00 00 00)
assert(game+82607,0a)
assert(game+826FF,68 36 01 00 00)
assert(game+8273B,68 36 01 00 00)
// NOTE: this line used to be
//     assert(cave+3FF0,4c 45 50 52 41 43 33 3a 46 49 58 45 44 3a 31 00)
// i.e. the "LEPRAC3:FIXED:1" version marker the ORIGINAL practice mod kept at
// cave+0x3FF0.  cea's assert() does not only CHECK -- it WRITES the byte list
// into the image.  Our own data section has since grown over that range, so
// the write was silently stamping those 15 bytes across
// OVL_STAGE / OVL_TXTCNT / SEED_USED / OVL_PREV_SEEDSW / OVL_TYPE_ON, turning
// OVL_STAGE into 0x4C000000 ("...\0\0\0L") -- and ovl_mirror dereferenced it
// on the very first frame.  That was the crash.  The marker is preserved as
// ordinary labelled data at the END of our block instead; see LEPRAC_MARK.
